<!--
  The pallet and the solar modules standing on it.

  The modules stand on edge, side by side like books on a shelf: each rests
  on one long side, its glass facing the arm (-X). The whole pallet is tilted
  back by 10 degrees, deck and back rest together: the deck slopes down away
  from the arm and the back rest stands at right angles to it. Each module
  stands square on the deck and so leans back by the same 10 degrees, against
  the module behind it; the last one leans on the back rest.

  Why tilt the whole pallet rather than lean the modules on a level deck: on
  the tilted deck gravity pulls every module down the slope, into the stack
  and the back rest, so the stack stands on normal forces alone. No friction
  has to carry a steady load. That matters in MuJoCo, where friction is soft:
  a contact under a steady sideways load slips slowly, so a stack held by
  friction creeps. A level deck would need friction under every bottom edge
  to stop the leaning modules kicking out at the foot.

  The pallet body is a mocap body: the physics holds it fixed, but its pose
  is in mjData (mocap_pos, mocap_quat), so a scene generator can move it for
  each trial without changing the model (see src/pallet.h). Its origin is on
  the floor, directly under the centre of the front module's glass face.

  Where the pallet stands: 1.95 m from the arm along +X. That number is
  written once, in the frame that holds both the pallet and the modules
  below; everything inside that frame is relative to the pallet origin.
  (The modules have free joints, so they cannot be children of the pallet
  body; a frame is only a shift applied when the model is built, so they
  stay children of the world.)

  The modules are module_0 (front, nearest the arm) to module_29 (back). Each
  is a rigid box with its origin at its centre: +x along the long side, +y
  along the short side, +z out of the glass. The glass is the +z face, at
  z = +0.0175. Standing on the pallet, +x points to world -Y (to the right as
  seen from the arm), +y points up the lean and +z toward the arm.

  Numbers, relative to the pallet origin (s = sin 10 deg = 0.173648,
  c = cos 10 deg = 0.984808):
    module_0 glass centre          (0, 0, 0.75); in the world (1.95, 0, 0.75)
    pitch from module to module    0.035, one thickness: they are built
                                   touching, so there is no gap to close
    bottom edge of module_0 glass  (-0.55 s, 0, 0.75 - 0.55 c)
                                   = (-0.095506, 0, 0.208356); the deck
                                   surface passes through this line

  Contact settings, the same for pallet and modules:
    solref 0.005 1   A contact pushes back with a time constant of 5 ms
                     (MuJoCo's default is 20 ms). The stiffer contacts let
                     the stack find its rest within a second; with 20 ms it
                     was still settling 0.7 mm and 1 mrad further between
                     1 s and 15 s. 5 ms is 2.5 timesteps, just above the 2
                     that MuJoCo needs.
    solimp 0.95 0.99 0.001
                     How much of that stiffness acts: 95 % at first touch,
                     99 % beyond 1 mm. Firmer than the default 0.9 0.95 and
                     what took the remaining drift down to under a micron.
    friction         Sliding friction only matters (condim 3, the default:
                     no torsional or rolling friction). Where two geoms meet
                     MuJoCo uses the larger of their two values.
-->
<mujoco>
  <default>
    <!-- Pallet steel. A module's aluminium frame on it: 0.6. Only the deck
         and the back rest touch the modules. -->
    <default class="pallet">
      <geom type="box" friction="0.6 0.005 0.0001" solref="0.005 1"
            solimp="0.95 0.99 0.001" rgba="0.45 0.35 0.25 1"/>
      <!-- Drawn only: touches nothing. -->
      <default class="pallet_visual">
        <geom contype="0" conaffinity="0" rgba="0.35 0.27 0.2 1"/>
      </default>
    </default>

    <!-- One module: 30 kg, 2.3 x 1.1 x 0.035 m (size is half of each), dark
         blue. One module's back on the next one's glass: friction 0.4. -->
    <default class="module">
      <geom type="box" size="1.15 0.55 0.0175" mass="30" friction="0.4 0.005 0.0001"
            solref="0.005 1" solimp="0.95 0.99 0.001" rgba="0.12 0.16 0.35 1"/>
    </default>
  </default>

  <asset>
    <!-- The stand under the deck. Seen from the side a right triangle: as
         tall as the deck at the front, nothing at the back. Its top is 1 mm
         under the deck so the two do not flicker where they meet. -->
    <mesh name="pallet_stand"
          vertex="-0.1966 -1.2 0        -0.1966 1.2 0
                  -0.1966 -1.2 0.2099   -0.1966 1.2 0.2099
                   0.9753 -1.2 0         0.9753 1.2 0
                   0.9753 -1.2 0.0033    0.9753 1.2 0.0033"/>
  </asset>

  <worldbody>
    <!-- The pallet origin: the one place that says how far from the arm the
         pallet stands. -->
    <frame pos="1.95 0 0">
      <body name="pallet" pos="0 0 0" mocap="true" childclass="pallet">
        <geom name="pallet_stand" class="pallet_visual" type="mesh" mesh="pallet_stand"/>

        <!-- The deck frame: origin on the deck surface under the bottom edge
             of module_0's glass, x down the slope (away from the arm), z out
             of the deck. Tilted 10 degrees (0.174533 rad) about Y. -->
        <frame pos="-0.095506 0 0.208356" euler="0 0.174533 0">
          <!-- A 15 mm plate, its top at z = 0, from 0.10 in front of module_0
               to the back of the back rest. -->
          <geom name="pallet_deck" size="0.595 1.25 0.0075" pos="0.495 0 -0.0075"/>
          <!-- 40 mm thick and 1.0 m tall. Its front face touches the back of
               module_29, at 30 x 0.035 = 1.05. -->
          <geom name="pallet_back" size="0.02 1.25 0.5" pos="1.07 0 0.5"/>
        </frame>
      </body>

      <!-- The modules. The frame is module_0: its centre is half a thickness
           behind the glass centre (0, 0, 0.75), and xyaxes gives its +x and +y
           in world coordinates: +x = -Y, +y = (s, 0, c). Each next module is
           one pitch further back, along -z. -->
      <frame pos="0.017234 0 0.746961" xyaxes="0 -1 0 0.173648 0 0.984808">
        <body name="module_0" pos="0 0 0.000"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_1" pos="0 0 -0.035"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_2" pos="0 0 -0.070"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_3" pos="0 0 -0.105"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_4" pos="0 0 -0.140"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_5" pos="0 0 -0.175"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_6" pos="0 0 -0.210"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_7" pos="0 0 -0.245"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_8" pos="0 0 -0.280"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_9" pos="0 0 -0.315"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_10" pos="0 0 -0.350"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_11" pos="0 0 -0.385"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_12" pos="0 0 -0.420"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_13" pos="0 0 -0.455"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_14" pos="0 0 -0.490"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_15" pos="0 0 -0.525"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_16" pos="0 0 -0.560"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_17" pos="0 0 -0.595"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_18" pos="0 0 -0.630"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_19" pos="0 0 -0.665"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_20" pos="0 0 -0.700"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_21" pos="0 0 -0.735"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_22" pos="0 0 -0.770"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_23" pos="0 0 -0.805"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_24" pos="0 0 -0.840"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_25" pos="0 0 -0.875"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_26" pos="0 0 -0.910"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_27" pos="0 0 -0.945"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_28" pos="0 0 -0.980"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
        <body name="module_29" pos="0 0 -1.015"><freejoint/><geom class="module"/></body>
      </frame>
    </frame>
  </worldbody>
</mujoco>
